 65	/**
 66	 * Wires all server components together, starts listening, and kicks off the
 67	 * background polling loop.
 68	 *
 69	 * The returned promise resolves once the server is actually listening on the
 70	 * chosen port (i.e. after the `listening` event fires).
 71	 *
 72	 * If the port is already in use (`EADDRINUSE`), the promise rejects with a
 73	 * descriptive `Error` and an actionable log message is printed to stderr.
 74	 *
 75	 * Calling `startServer()` while a server is already running throws
 76	 * synchronously.
 77	 *
 78	 * Internally creates an `ErrorLogManager` shared across all subsystems
 79	 * (WorkspaceOrchestrator, BranchOrchestrator, PollingManager, and Router);
 80	 * no external reference is returned.
